cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenRoIS in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
title: >-
  OpenRoIS: Open-Source Middleware Implementing the OMG Robotic Interaction
  Service (RoIS) Framework 2.0
abstract: >-
  OpenRoIS is a community-driven open-source middleware that implements the
  OMG Robotic Interaction Service (RoIS) Framework 2.0. It provides a recursive
  engine that realizes the main and sub HRI Engine roles, a single protocol in
  which the RoIS method catalog over JSON-RPC 2.0 and WebSocket is the only
  interface at every hop, a single-source-of-truth type pipeline in which
  Python models are exported to JSON Schema and generated into TypeScript and
  C# types, client SDKs for JavaScript, Python, and Unity, a component SDK, a
  browser inspector, and a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for AI agents,
  so that one service application, scripted or an AI agent, can address
  physical robots, virtual avatars, and digital services.
authors:
